vember 13 low on record (124 years since 1893).","t_rec":"Riverside has nearly stopped setting record lows","p_rec":"If Riverside's climate weren't changing, every year would have the same chance of holding a daily record. Since 2000, Riverside has set <strong class=\"sig\">no standing record lows at all</strong>, far fewer than the 74 that chance alone would give, and <strong>94 record highs</strong>, more than the 74 that chance alone would give. The 1910s hold the most record highs of any decade (51). Riverside's all-time high is 118\u00b0F, on June 16, 1917.","t_chg":"Riverside's days and nights both warmed. Nights warmed faster.","p_chg":"Across 116 complete years: Riverside's average low has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.76\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.68 to +0.83), about +9.9\u00b0F since 1894. Riverside's average high has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.14\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.07 to +0.22), about +1.9\u00b0F since 1894.","t_mon":"Lows rose in all 12 months. Highs rose in 7 of 12 months.","t_rain":"Rain: no clear long-term change","p_rain":"Riverside's yearly precipitation shows no clear long-term change (\u22120.21 inches per decade, a range that includes zero). The 1991\u20132020 normal is 9.5 inches a year. The wettest year was 1983 (22.94 in); the driest, 2013 (3.40 in). Riverside almost never sees snow (the 1991\u20132020 average is 0.0 inches a winter), so there's no snowfall chart.","show_snow":false,"sig_bars":{"lo":true,"hi":false},"t_year":"2026 so far: 10 daily record highs, no daily record lows"}}